// The closure runtime (docs/SPEC.md 1.1.1), printed after the prelude and
// before the declarations, because the declarations name IdFn. `linkage` is
// "static " in a program's own C and "" in the external-linkage runtime the
// LLVM target links (runtime/extern.id), the same text with the same two
// spellings of one word. Every function value is a pointer to an IdFn: fn
// takes the object first, raw is the plain function (0 for a closure), and the
// n captured cells follow the header, 8 bytes each as a list cell is.

emit_closure_rt(string linkage) {
  emit_line("#define ID_CLO " + linkage);
  emit_line((import c_clo_types));
  emit_line((import c_clo_ops));
} chain (string linkage) {
  emit_line((import c_clo_cmp));
  fv_init();
} return void;
("static "):() then calls emit_line:("#define ID_CLO static ") then calls fv_init:[1]
(""):() then calls emit_line:("#define ID_CLO ") then calls fv_init:[1]

